    introduction: 'The capstone combines entity modeling, relational keys, constraints, SQL, and transactions in one small library design.',
    theory: 'A useful database design starts by deciding what the system must remember over time. A library needs books or editions, members, and loan events. One title may have several physical copies, and one member may borrow many copies at different times. The model must distinguish a catalog record from a copy and a current loan from its historical record. Define key fields, required relationships, status values, and rules such as one active loan per copy before building the schema.',
